      "text": "To find the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to \\(15 \\pmod{22}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the largest 4-digit integer, which is 9999.\n2. Determine the remainder when 9999 is divided by 22.\n3. Adjust the number so that it is congruent to 15 modulo 22 by subtracting the difference between 9999 modulo 22 and 15.\n\nWe start by calculating \\(9999 \\mod 22\\):\n\\[9999 \\div 22 \\approx 454.545\\]\nThe integer part of the division is 454, so we calculate:\n\\[9999 - 454 \\times 22 = 9999 - 9988 = 11\\]\nThus, \\(9999 \\equiv 11 \\pmod{22}\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the largest number less than or equal to 9999 that is congruent to 15 modulo 22. We do this by subtracting the difference between 11 and 15 from 9999:\n\\[9999 - (15 - 11) = 9999 - 4 = 9995\\]\nThus, the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to \\(15 \\pmod{22}\\) is \\(\\boxed{9995}\\).",
